title: "Delete the authenticated account"
icon: x
description: "Delete the authenticated account: deleteAccount in the TypeScript, Python and Rust clients."
---

`DELETE /v1/account`

Deletes the authenticated account and returns its account tombstone. The operation is rejected while the account still owns organizations; transfer or close those organizations before retrying. This endpoint acts on the caller's account and does not accept another account's identifier.

<Tabs>
<Tab title="TypeScript">
```typescript TypeScript
photon.account.delete(input?: DeleteAccountInput, options?: RequestOptions): Promise<DeleteAccountOutput>
```
</Tab>
<Tab title="Python">
```python Python
photon.account.delete(input: DeleteAccountInput | None = None) -> models.Account
```
</Tab>
<Tab title="Rust">
```rust Rust
client.delete_account().await -> Result<ResponseValue<types::Account>, Error<DeleteAccountError>>
```
</Tab>
</Tabs>

<RequestExample>
```typescript TypeScript
import { Photon } from "@photon-ai/api";

const photon = new Photon({
  headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${process.env.PHOTON_API_TOKEN}` },
});
const result = await photon.account.delete();
```

```python Python
import os

from photon_api import Photon

photon = Photon(headers={"Authorization": f"Bearer {os.environ['PHOTON_API_TOKEN']}"})
result = photon.account.delete()
```

```rust Rust
use photon_ai_api::{Credential, PhotonClientBuilder, SecretString};

let token = std::env::var("PHOTON_API_TOKEN")?;
let client = PhotonClientBuilder::new()
    .credential("accountServiceKey", Credential::Bearer(SecretString::from(token)))
    .build()?;
let result = client
    .delete_account()
    .await
    .map_err(|error| format!("{error:?}"))?
    .into_inner();
```

</RequestExample>

